Ghadirian</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Gorodetzky</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberfroid</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahon</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartsch</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Day</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oesophageal cancer studies in the Caspian Littoral of Iran: some residual results, including opium use as a risk factor</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>1985</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>593</fpage><lpage>597</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||35|593||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hecht</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tobacco carcinogens, their biomarkers and tobacco-induced cancer</article-title><source>Nat Rev Cancer</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>744</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Nat Rev Cancer||3|733||bib12|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hewer</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghadirian</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Castegnaro</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Malaveille</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartsch</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Day</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ingested mutagens from opium and tobacco pyrolysis products and cancer of the oesophagus</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1978</year><volume>2</volume><